@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-token
# Use an ACTIVE project and a sellable product with enough stock in a disposable DB.
@projectId = replace-with-active-project-id
@productId = replace-with-project-product-id
@orderId = replace-with-created-order-id
# Change keys when starting a fresh test run; keep them identical for retry checks.
@namedKey = operator-name-test-1
@fallbackKey = operator-name-test-2

### Named operator — 201; operator_name is "มายด์", staff is the logged-in account
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{namedKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":"  มายด์  ","buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Normalized retry — 200, Idempotency-Replayed: true; same order, no extra stock reduction
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{namedKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":"มายด์","buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Changed operator with the same key — 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{namedKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":"กิตติ","buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Omitted operator — 201; operator_name equals staff.full_name; DB value is NULL
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{fallbackKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Explicit null retries the omitted request — 200 with original staff snapshot
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{fallbackKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":null,"buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Blank also retries the omitted request — 200; same operator name
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{fallbackKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":"   ","buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Invalid type — 400 VALIDATION_ERROR; no order or stock changes
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: operator-invalid-type
Content-Type: application/json

{"operator_name":123,"buyer":{"gender":"PREFER_NOT_TO_SAY"},"items":[{"product_id":{{productId}},"variant_id":null,"quantity":1}],"payment":{"method":"REAL_MONEY","received_amount":"999999.00","no_change":false}}

### Detail — 200; same resolved operator name as checkout
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### History — 200; named and fallback orders retain their individual names
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Excel — final column is Operator Name; original Staff Name/Email columns remain
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/orders/export
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Automated tests also cover the 100/101 Unicode character limit, QR checkout,
# raw NULL storage, account renames, stock actors, old fingerprint compatibility,
# pre-migration rows, and migration rollback/reapply on an isolated database.
